= Genomics =

== Overview ==
'''Genomics''' is the field of biology that studies genomes as large-scale systems, including their sequences, genes, regulatory elements, variation, organization, and interactions.

A genome is the complete genetic material of an organism or cell under a specified biological definition. Genomics often analyzes many genes or genome-wide features simultaneously rather than focusing on one locus at a time.

Genomic research includes genome sequencing and assembly, variant analysis, comparative genomics, functional genomics, epigenomics, population genomics, and integration with other molecular data.

Genomics depends heavily on bioinformatics because genome-scale datasets are too large and structured for manual analysis alone. It remains a biological field, not simply a synonym for sequence computation.

== Boundaries ==
* genomics ≠ genetics
* genomics ≠ genome sequencing only
* genome-scale data ≠ biological interpretation by itself

